  ('105', 105, false, 'IT', '**"Waived" fee status in the portal (requested by the President 2026-10-06 — "we will need it more often").** Today a waived month is faked as a payment with method "other" and a WAIVED reference (see Safiha''s September), which inflates "Total received" and must be manually excluded from QBO matching. Build: a `waived` payment method (or a separate waiver record) on `payments`, a "Waive month" button beside "Record payment" in Admin → Fees capturing month, reason and approver, a distinct grey "Waived" pill (vs green Paid / red Unpaid) on the Fees page, parent fees view and dashboard tile, waived amounts excluded from "Total received" and from reconciliation/Reports CSV totals (own column), and the audit log entry. Migrate the Safiha 09-2026 row to the new status when it ships. Dev first per [docs/dev-to-prod.md](docs/dev-to-prod.md); President approves wording/UI before prod. Pairs with the scholarship policy (#90) — waivers are what the policy will authorize', 'Claude builds → Muneeb (President) approves', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('104', 104, false, 'Students & Families', '**Complete the withdrawal of the departing students (10007 — family circumstances; 10006 — too young for class; President 2026-10-06) plus a third added 2026-10-09: 10009 (Pre-K, not attending; last attendance mark 2026-09-15), archived and withdrawn the same way.** Done: 10007 and 10006 ARCHIVED in the portal. **2026-10-09: the President chose to wait for the one-click Suspend / Withdraw button (#112) instead of running the SQL by hand; do all three with it once it is live**. Remaining: withdraw all three with the button (archive + enrollment withdrawn with exit date and reason + fee plan closed; default: unpaid September for 10006/10007 waived, no back-charge), then tell the families', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-23', '2026-10-23', 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('103', 103, false, 'Development', '**501(c)(3) donation acknowledgment letters for September gifts ≥ $250** (IRS written-acknowledgment requirement; needed before the donor files their return, best practice promptly): (1) **$5,000 counter deposit of 09-11** — President names the donor(s) and whether it was one gift or several; (2) **$500 Zelle donation of 09-21** (donor named in the bank feed and in the letter). Claude drafts both letters (school letterhead, EIN 39-2254583, gift date/amount, "no goods or services were provided" clause) as soon as the $5,000 donor is named; President signs and sends. Smaller September donors ($150/$125/$50/$50/$25) get a simple thank-you — optional, can ride along. **2026-10-12:** generator `scripts/make-donation-letter.py` added; the $500 letter is drafted in `11_Donations & Grants/02. 2026/02. General Donations/Acknowledgments/` — donor''s name confirmed by the President as the bank shows it, ready to sign and send. **$5,000 of 09-11: one business donor (named by the President 2026-10-13), cheque, general donation — letter drafted the same day** in the same Acknowledgments folder. **Left:** the $500 donor''s spelling — President awaiting confirmation (2026-10-13), then regenerate if needed; President signs and sends both letters; add the donor name to the two September donations in QBO', 'Muneeb (President) names donor → Claude drafts → President signs', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('34', 34, false, 'Finance', 'TechSoup: create the org account and request donated QBO Plus ($80/yr) now that the 501(c)(3) letter exists; plan the company-file migration and cancellation of the $140/mo plan **Unblocked 2026-09-25: letter on file.** **Plan agreed 2026-10-13:** (1) President registers Falah Academy on TechSoup now (school Gmail, EIN, IRS letter; validation days–2 weeks); (2) request the QBO Plus donation, President pays the $80 admin fee; (3) new company file starts 2027-01-01 — Claude sets up accounts, classes, opening balances from the closed 2026 books; (4) 2026 stays in the old file through the December close and January 1099/W-2 work; (5) cancel the paid plan about Feb 2027 after exporting reports to `08_Financials`. TechSoup FAQ (checked 2026-10-13): the offer **cannot be applied to the existing account** — new company file confirmed; **Payroll is not part of the donation**, so QBO Payroll must be bought from Intuit for the new file and set up again from 2027-01-01 (2026 W-2s filed from the old file). Choose **Plus** ($80/yr), not Advanced; request/activate it in early–mid December so the donated year starts near Jan 1. **2026-10-13: TechSoup account created (login = school Gmail) and Falah Academy submitted for validation** — 501(c)(3), EIN 39-2254583, IRS-letter address (13028 SE 231st Way, Kent 98031), Schools/Colleges → Private school, budget $96,000 (President''s estimate), role Executive Director; no match existed; TechSoup now verifies with the IRS — **up to 7 business days (by about 2026-10-22)**, result by e-mail to the school Gmail; status also in the TechSoup account (docs/accounts.md row). Next: when validated, put the December QBO Plus request on the calendar **2026-10-14: TechSoup VALIDATED Falah Academy (e-mail "Your Organization Has Been Qualified", 2:00 PM, school Gmail).** Next: request QBO Plus ($80, President pays) in early–mid December (calendar reminder 2026-12-07), activate near Jan 1; new company file 2027-01-01', 'Muneeb (President) requests in Dec → Claude migrates', '2026-12-10', '2026-12-10', 'Waiting', null, '[{"name": "2026-03-31_IRS_501c3_Determination_Letter_(effective_2025-05-23)_FalahAcademy_EIN39-2254583.pdf", "path": "34/2026-03-31_IRS_501c3_Determination_Letter_-effective_2025-05-23-_FalahAcademy_EIN39-2254583.pdf", "size": 136699}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('40', 40, false, 'Legal & Compliance', 'Insurance: general liability quotes, or written confirmation Al Huda''s policy covers the school', 'Muneeb (President)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('41', 41, false, 'Legal & Compliance', '**WA Charities Program registration (RCW 19.09) — checked 2026-10-12: registration IS required.** Neither exemption in WAC 434-120-100 fits (the under-$50k one needs an all-volunteer organization with no paid staff — Falah has W-2 teachers; the church one covers only churches and integrated auxiliaries — Falah is a separate 170(b)(1)(A)(ii) school). Must register before public solicitation (flyers, Zelle QR, sponsorships #89, matching gifts #88). Filing pack with every answer the form needs: `records/09_Audits & Compliance Reviews/2026-10-12_WA_Charities_Registration_Filing_Pack.md`. **President:** file in CCFS (ccfs.sos.wa.gov → Charities → register), about $60, upload the 501(c)(3) letter; then Claude files the confirmation and adds the yearly renewal to DEADLINES. **Filed and paid 2026-10-12** ($60, work order 2026101200796330; receipt in `09_Audits & Compliance Reviews/01. State Reviews`; renewal added to DEADLINES, first due 2027-11-30). Waiting for the SOS approval email to the school Gmail (about 5 business days), then file it and close; the $60 was paid with the school VISA (…0039, confirmed 2026-10-12): when it appears in the QBO bank feed, categorize it as Taxes & Licenses, memo "WA SOS charity registration WO 2026101200796330" (do not also add it by hand)', 'Muneeb (President) → SOS approval', '2026-10-19', '2026-10-19', 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
