  ('50', 50, false, 'Academics', 'Confirm 157 school days satisfies Red Comet / ALE', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('143', 143, false, 'Development', '**Google Ad Grants — up to $10,000 a month of free Google Search ads for nonprofits.** **Step 0 (added 2026-10-14): eligibility — Google for Nonprofits excludes schools, so Falah (IRS school class) is probably ineligible; confirm with Google first (see #91) and close this task if so.** Steps: (1) Google for Nonprofits account for Falah Academy (via the school Gmail; verification through Percent, uses EIN 39-2254583 and the 501(c)(3) letter — schools may need to qualify under the nonprofit, not the education, track; check eligibility first); (2) activate Ad Grants, create the Ads account under the school Gmail; (3) link GA4 (G-V6DNKDR9Z8) and set conversions (admissions form, donate page, volunteer form); (4) Claude drafts campaigns: admissions (Kent / Auburn / Renton Islamic school, Pre-K – Grade 1), donations, volunteers; (5) keep the compliance rules (5% CTR, monthly login, conversion tracking) so the grant isn''t suspended. Needs #51 GA owner first; ties to #91 (Google for Nonprofits)', 'Muneeb (President) applies → Claude builds campaigns', '2026-12-15', '2026-12-15', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('141', 141, false, 'IT', '**Move the Red Comet (Buzz) login from the President''s personal Outlook to a school e-mail** (President 2026-10-13: not urgent, can be next school year). Ask Red Comet support (alesupport@redcomet.com) to change the account e-mail to falahacademywa@gmail.com or add it as a second admin, so student records are not tied to a personal address; update `docs/accounts.md`', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2027-06-30', '2027-06-30', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('142', 142, false, 'IT', '**School-owned OneDrive for the records** (President 2026-10-13: not urgent, can be next year). `records/` (OneDrive `03 Falah Academy`, includes student and staff files) sits on the President''s personal Microsoft account. Options: (a) a free Microsoft account for the school (5 GB — likely too small); (b) **Microsoft 365 A1 for Education** (free for qualifying schools — the nonprofit grant excludes schools, see #91) or Google Workspace for Education storage; Microsoft 365 Business Basic via the nonprofit grant only if Microsoft accepts Falah (1 TB OneDrive per user, school-owned, ties in with #91 in-kind programs). Then move the folder, re-point the hub `records` junction and the generator scripts, and update `docs/accounts.md`', 'Muneeb (President) decides → Claude moves', '2027-06-30', '2027-06-30', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('66', 66, false, 'Marketing', '**Entrance signage:** only an 11x17 banner marks the school at Al Huda. Get Al Huda''s OK, then order a portable A-frame or yard sign (about 24x36 in: logo, "Falah Academy", "Mon–Thu 9:00–2:00") for school days; check Kent''s portable-sign rules. While talking to Al Huda: ask them to correct the "Islamic School (Dugsi) Mon–Thu 9:00–1:00" line on alhudaislamiccenter.com/islamic-school (dugsi is weekends) and add a link to falahacademywa.org (was #25). Also photograph the entrance with the banner for the Google cover photo (#24)', 'Muneeb (President), Al Huda admin (Someone else)', 'next school visit', null, 'Parked', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('67', 67, false, 'Legal & Compliance', '**File the 2027 WA SOS annual report** (CCFS, UBI 605 907 024; window opens 2026-12-02, expiration 2027-05-31; $20; Express filing works while status is Active). Save the report + receipt to `records/01_Corporate & Legal/03. Registrations & Certificates`', 'Muneeb (President)', '2027-04-30', '2027-04-30', 'Not started', null, '[{"name": "2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Filed_UBI-605907024.pdf", "path": "67/2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Filed_UBI-605907024.pdf", "size": 298079}, {"name": "2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Note.md", "path": "67/2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Note.md", "size": 1287}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('69', 69, false, 'IT', '**Admissions: sibling fee plan + payment status — SHIPPED to prod 2026-09-28 (dev `5150fa3`).** Next to the "Sibling enrolled" badge the card shows a pill per sibling ("$300/mo · Sep paid ✓" / "Sep unpaid · 1 mo behind" / "starts …"); the dialog lists months paid of months owed this school year and the last payment date; the Monthly fee box defaults to **$200** with a "family rate" hint when a paying sibling is found (still editable). No SQL needed. Mark done once the President has seen it on a real applicant with an enrolled sibling.', 'Muneeb (Principal) verifies', '2026-11-30', '2026-11-30', 'Ready', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('84', 84, false, 'Academics', '**Red Comet weekly check-ins for all six Red Comet students (KG 3, Grade 1 2, Grade 3 1 — every KG+ student is with Red Comet; Pre-K is not).** Washington ALE rules from Red Comet''s orientation e-mails (two families forwarded theirs, 09-10 and 09-17, starred in the school Gmail under *Families & Admissions* + *Partners/Red Comet & MESBA*): a weekly attendance assignment in **every course**, a weekly login with visible progress, the Written Student Learning Plan completed first (it unlocks the course), Red Comet''s calendar not the school''s, withdrawal after 10 days counts as failed for grades 9–12. **Done so far:** the KG teacher received the three KG students'' Red Comet logins from the President on 10-01 (Gmail *Sent*, "Password and urls"). **Decide and do:** (1) the class teacher does the weekly check-in for her Red Comet students — confirm the Grade 1 / Grade 3 teacher also has her students'' logins; (2) where it is logged: portal Class Updates form or Red Comet''s own log, one place; (3) confirm all six have logged in and finished their Learning Plan, and that no weekly assignment is already overdue (school started 08-26, logins issued 09-10 onward); (4) reply to the two families who forwarded their e-mails and ask all six families to change the plain-text passwords once logged in. The teacher guide #87 is done (D-row); once (1)–(2) are decided, add a short schedule box to it: who checks in, which day (check-ins are due Saturday 11 PM), when to escalate to the Principal, Red Comet support alesupport@redcomet.com / redcomet.org/ale-faq. Note: since 2026-10-08 Claude enters workbook answers and weekly check-ins in Buzz with the President (see `17_Students/02. 2026 - 2027/05. Red Comet Workbook/`). (Closed by mistake 2026-10-04 and reopened the same evening.)', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-15', '2026-10-15', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('88', 88, false, 'Development', '**Employer matching gifts — register the school so parents'' donations are doubled by their employers.** Microsoft, Boeing, T-Mobile, Costco, Starbucks, Expedia and others match employee gifts to 501(c)(3)s (Microsoft up to about $15,000 per employee a year, plus $25 per volunteer hour). Steps: (1) Claude prepares the pack: EIN 39-2254583, determination letter, mission text, W-9, bank details for ACH, logo; (2) President creates the school''s profile on **Benevity Causes** (causes.benevity.org) and **YourCause / Blackbaud** (solutions.yourcause.com/nonprofits) — account creation is the President''s step, Claude cannot do it; also claim the school on **Charity Navigator** and **GuideStar/Candid** so the portals verify faster; (3) once approved, Claude drafts the WhatsApp message and a Jumu''ah announcement for Al Huda: "ask HR whether your company matches gifts; donate through your company portal and the school receives double"; (4) record each matched gift in QBO as a donation (class Tuition Program or Scholarship). Needs #41 settled first **Progress 2026-10-11: Benevity Causes account created with the school Gmail and the listing claimed — cause ID 840-392254583; account completion 40%.** Left on Benevity: Certification + Declaration pages, **Donation Method = electronic transfer** (else quarterly paper cheques with a fee), profile (logo, mission, description, website, address); then YourCause, Charity Navigator and Candid. **2026-10-13: profile and declarations being completed by the President; EFT chosen; bank verification blocked — BofA''s online direct-deposit form does not show "Falah Academy", so the President is getting a signed account verification letter at a BofA branch (holder Falah Academy, full account + routing number, letterhead, signed) to upload to Benevity.** Parent/Jumu''ah announcement waits for the WA Charities approval (#41).', 'Claude prepares → Muneeb (President) registers', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('89', 89, false, 'Development', '**Business sponsorship package for the fundraiser.** Claude drafts in `marketing/fundraiser-2026/sponsorship/`: (a) one-page tier sheet — Bronze $500, Silver $1,000, Gold $2,500, Platinum $5,000 — each giving name, logo, slogan and contact details on the flyer, event banner, website sponsors section and monthly newsletter (**acknowledgement only: no prices, no praise, no "call today"**, so every dollar stays a tax-free qualified sponsorship payment and the sponsor can deduct it); (b) a one-page sponsor letter signed by the President with the 501(c)(3) line and EIN; (c) a prospect list in `records/13_Marketing & Communication/` — Muslim-owned businesses in Kent, Renton, Tukwila, Seattle (restaurants, grocers, physicians, dentists, realtors, lawyers, car dealers) and the Islamic-finance / halal brands that sponsor Islamic schools: Saturna Capital / Amana Funds (Bellingham), Guidance Residential, UIF, Ijara CDC, Crescent Foods, Saffron Road, Zabihah; (d) a sponsors block for the website and the deck (#59). President reviews, then approaches the local businesses in person and the brands by e-mail. Every sponsorship over $250 gets a written acknowledgement letter for the sponsor''s taxes (`scripts/make-donation-letter.py`). **2026-10-13: not urgent (President) — moved to 2026-12-01; approach sponsors only after the WA Charities registration (#41) is approved; fundraiser date/venue needed for the tier sheet**', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (President) approaches', '2026-12-01', '2026-12-01', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('90', 90, false, 'Development', '**Need-based scholarship policy + "Sponsor a student" ($300 a month or $3,000 a school year).** The website advertises need-based scholarships but no written policy or fund exists. Claude drafts a one-page policy (who qualifies, how a family applies, who decides — President + Treasurer, no board member''s own family, award = partial or full tuition for one school year, renewed yearly, confidential) and a sponsor-a-student one-pager for #89; the board adopts the policy by written consent together with #4; sponsor money is tracked in QBO under a *Scholarship Fund* class and awards are recorded in the portal as fee-plan adjustments. File in `records/10_Policies & Governance/`', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (President) + board adopt', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('91', 91, false, 'Development', '**Free in-kind programs now open with the 501(c)(3) letter:** Google for Nonprofits (Workspace, Ad Grants $10,000/month in search ads, YouTube) — apply through TechSoup validation (#34); Microsoft 365 nonprofit grant (free Business Basic seats) and Azure credits; **Fred Meyer Community Rewards** (families link their rewards card, the school gets a share of their grocery spend, nothing to the family); **Box Tops for Education** (enrol the school, families scan receipts in the app). Claude prepares each application and the two-line WhatsApp asks for families; President submits (accounts and consents are his step) **Update 2026-10-14 (moved to December by the President):** TechSoup validated Falah 2026-10-14 (#34). **Eligibility catch:** Google for Nonprofits and Microsoft''s nonprofit grants both **exclude schools / academic institutions** and send them to their education programs — Falah''s IRS class is a school (170(b)(1)(A)(ii)), so it is probably ineligible for Google for Nonprofits (and therefore Ad Grants #143) and the Microsoft nonprofit grant. **Education route instead:** (a) **Google Workspace for Education Fundamentals** — free for qualifying K–12 schools: school-domain e-mail @falahacademywa.org for all staff and students, Drive, Classroom, Meet, admin console, large pooled storage; (b) **Microsoft 365 A1 for Education** — free, OneDrive for a school-owned records store (#142). Both normally require the school to be state-recognized: **first confirm whether Falah is on Washington''s approved private school list (State Board of Education)**; if not, ask Google/Microsoft what proof they accept, and only then try the nonprofit programs. (For reference, Google Workspace for Nonprofits would give up to 2,000 free accounts; aliases/groups such as info@, admissions@, donate@ do not use accounts — the school needs about 5–8 real ones.) Fred Meyer Community Rewards and Box Tops are unaffected and can be done any time', 'Claude prepares → Muneeb (President) submits', '2026-12-15', '2026-12-15', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('92', 92, false, 'HR', '**Volunteer program — set it up before the first volunteer walks in.** **Two volunteers applied through the website on 2026-10-10 (both in Admin → Volunteers, status New)** — they are the ones to screen first. (The six teaching applicants answered on 10-04/05 are a separate matter, parked in #140.) Claude drafts: a one-page volunteer application (contact, availability, references, consent to a background check), the WA background check step (Washington State Patrol WATCH check, about $12 per person, plus the DCYF/national check if the volunteer is ever alone with children — ties to #42 Child Protection Policy), a one-page volunteer agreement (always under a teacher''s supervision, confidentiality of student information, photo rule, sign-in sheet), and a simple schedule template. Principal approves, then the two online applicants get the agreement with their visit date. File in `records/10_Policies & Governance/` and `records/16_Employees/00. Applicants & Waiting List/` **Drafts v1 ready 2026-10-05 (Claude):** four documents in `records/10_Policies & Governance/06. Volunteer Program/` as .docx + PDF — 01 Application Form, 02 Background Check Procedure (internal: references, WSP WATCH ≈ $12, nsopw.gov, fingerprint check only for unsupervised roles, decision rules, filing under `16_Employees/00. Volunteers/`), 03 Volunteer Agreement (never alone with a student, confidentiality, no photos, contact only via the school, reporting concerns), 04 Weekly Schedule + monthly Sign-in Sheet. Generator `scripts/make-volunteer-docs.py` (edit text there, re-run, Word makes the PDFs). **The live form already accepts applications (D50) and the WhatsApp call is drafted — approve these documents before posting it.** **2026-10-12:** Volunteer Agreement rewritten as an Islamic "amanah" agreement on the President''s wording (no supervision/medicine/sign-in clauses; speaking-up, privacy with hadith, images, families incl. WhatsApp, adab, screening consent), professional layout with boxed signature fields; blank templates of all four documents copied to `records/16_Employees/00. Volunteers/00. Templates/` with a filing README (one folder per volunteer for the signed agreement, WATCH result, references). **Waiting:** the President brings the first signed agreement; Claude files it and sets the volunteer to Active. **Principal:** review, decide 18+ only or 16–17 with parent signature, call both references of the two online applicants, then send 03 with their visit date **2026-10-13 (President):** interest list changed to Classroom support: Pre-K – Grade 1 · Islamic Studies · Reading & writing · Math & science · Art, PE or activities · Office & admissions help · Events & fundraising · Library & learning materials · Other (with text) — Grade 3 is never named on forms or ads; WATCH, nsopw.gov registry search and fingerprint check taken out for now (→ #139), screening = application + disclosures + two references, volunteer never alone with a student. Docs regenerated; live form changed in dev (prod after approval). **2026-10-13 (President): (1) the four documents approved; (2) age rule = 16+, with a parent''s/guardian''s signature for 16–17 (form and documents already say this); (3) screening of both online applicants done.** Left: send the Volunteer Agreement with a visit date, signed at orientation; Claude files the signed agreements under `16_Employees/00. Volunteers/<name>/` and sets both to Active; WhatsApp volunteer call can now go out; portal screening checklist cut to 4 steps (references ×2, orientation, agreement) — live in dev (`4043954`) and prod (`0aba468`) 2026-10-13.', 'Muneeb (Principal) → volunteers sign', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('140', 140, false, 'HR', '**Teaching applicants'' waiting list — parked until January 2027 (President 2026-10-13).** Six teaching applicants (Arabic/Qur''an/Islamic Studies, assistant teacher, general teaching inquiries; applied 07-08 to 09-30) were answered on 2026-10-04/05 with waiting list + request for résumé and two references + a volunteer offer (D49; threads under *Hiring/Applications* in the school Gmail). None has replied yet. In January: check for replies, decide who to keep on the list against the 2027–28 staffing plan, and answer anyone who wrote in the meantime. Not part of the volunteer program (#92)', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2027-01-15', '2027-01-15', 'Parked', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('139', 139, false, 'HR', '**Introduce volunteer background checks (taken out of the volunteer program on 2026-10-13, President: "for now").** Plan for December 2026 / January 2027: open a WSP WATCH account under the school Gmail (about $12 per check, every two years, QBO Background Checks / Administration), nsopw.gov registry search (free), fingerprint WSP/FBI check for volunteers who may be alone with students; add the consent wording back to the paper application (`scripts/make-volunteer-docs.py`), the live form (`volunteer.html`, dev then prod) the Volunteer Agreement section 8, and the portal''s screening checklist (`CHECKS` in `platform-src/src/pages/admin/Volunteers.tsx` — the `watch` and `registry` steps were removed 2026-10-13; dates already saved under those keys are kept in the data); run the checks for every volunteer already active; ties to the Child Protection Policy (#42)', 'Muneeb (Principal) decides → Claude updates forms', '2026-12-31', '2026-12-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('93', 93, false, 'Students & Families', '**Special-needs student: written handling guidance for the teachers.** The student''s father will send the details (diagnosis, triggers, what helps, routines, emergency steps, who to call). When they arrive: Claude drafts a one-page classroom guidance sheet for the class teacher and the Pre-K assistant, the Principal reviews, the family confirms, and it goes into the student''s folder in `records/17_Students/` (not into the hub) and to the teachers only. Note in the portal student profile that guidance exists.', 'Muneeb (Principal); Claude drafts', 'when the father''s details arrive', null, 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('100', 100, false, 'IT', '**Automatic fee invoices and receipts to parents (requested by the President 2026-10-05).** Goal: no hand-written receipts. Proposed $0 design on what exists: (1) **Invoice e-mail on the 1st of each month** from the daily GitHub Action via Brevo — one per family, listing each child''s monthly fee and the family total, due by the 5th, how to pay (Zelle to the school Gmail, cheque, deposit), and a link to the Family Portal fees page; (2) **Receipt e-mail the moment a payment is posted** — triggered when a `payments` row is inserted (by the Zelle auto-post #78 or by the office), showing amount, date, method, children covered, month covered and the remaining balance, with a PDF receipt attached (generated in the Action, 501(c)(3) footer and EIN for the family''s records); (3) **reminder on the 8th** for anything still unpaid; (4) the Fees page gets a *Download receipt* button per payment and a *Statement* per school year. In-app notification mirrors each e-mail. QuickBooks stays the ledger — QBO invoices to families are **not** sent (would duplicate, and the rule is confirm-first). Needs: the Brevo template set, a `receipt_no` sequence on `payments`, Supabase phase SQL, Action schedule. Build in dev first; President approves the e-mail wording before anything goes to a real family. Depends on #78 being live in prod.', 'Claude builds → Muneeb (President) approves wording', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('107', 107, false, 'Finance', '**After the first payroll (10-29): confirm QuickBooks is really paying and filing.** Payroll → Payroll taxes → Payments must list the federal 941 deposit and the Washington ESD (UI, Paid Leave, WA Cares) and L&I withdrawals as *Scheduled* with dates; Filings → Coming up must show Q4 forms. If any agency is missing or says "you pay", open the Resolution center and e-mail Intuit the same day: the first state deposits for Q4 are due 2027-01-31 and the 941 deposit by 11-15 (monthly depositor). Also confirm each employee''s first pay stub shows WA Cares 0.58%, PFML and workers'' comp deductions.', 'Claude (Muneeb (accountant) signs in)', '2026-10-30', '2026-10-30', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('136', 136, false, 'Finance', '**PFML/WA Cares Q4 2026 wage report — confirm filed (due 2027-02-01; the school''s first with real wages, payroll from 10-29).** Expected path: QuickBooks files it automatically once the state e-file authorisation is active (#107 verifies that after the first payroll). In January: sign in to paidleave.wa.gov via SAW (no PIN needed — full access is permanent on the school''s login, Customer ID C605907024) → Wage Reporting → Quarterly Report Status → Q4 2026 must read *Submitted*. If it still says Due by mid-January, file manually on the portal (Submit a Wage Report → payroll via Manual Entry, wages and hours from QuickBooks payroll reports) before 02-01 and tell Intuit the authorisation is not working. Also check Payments for the premium due.', 'Claude (Muneeb (accountant) signs in)', '2027-01-20', '2027-01-20', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('144', 144, false, 'Development', '**$500 donor-advised-fund grant on its way by paper cheque (grant ID 29876066, "Annual gift", timing ASAP) — watch the mail, deposit, record, thank.** A donor directed it through his giving fund (likely Fidelity Charitable); the cheque goes to the address the fund has on file, probably the registered (home) address. When it arrives: President deposits via the BofA app; Claude records it in QBO as a grant from the fund sponsor (donor noted as advisor, class Tuition Program) and drafts a thank-you letter to the donor — **acknowledgement only, no tax-deductible language** (his deduction happened when he funded the fund); file the cheque image and letter in `records/11_Donations & Grants/02. 2026/`. If nothing arrives by 11-07, the President checks the fund''s status page or asks the donor to re-check the mailing address.', 'Muneeb (President) receives → Claude records', '2026-11-07', '2026-11-07', 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('110', 110, false, 'Marketing', '**Automate public posts on the Facebook page (FalahAcademyWA) — explore and recommend (requested by the President 2026-10-08, "not urgent but the sooner the better").** Questions to answer: (1) can **Muse AI** (the President''s suggestion) draft and schedule posts for us, what it costs and whether it needs admin access to the page; (2) the $0 alternatives — Meta Business Suite''s own scheduler (free, can queue weeks of posts), Buffer or Later free tiers, or our own GitHub Action posting through the Facebook Graph API from a content calendar in a Sheet, with Claude drafting the copy; (3) what gets posted automatically without a human eye: announcements and calendar events from the portal, the volunteer and enrollment calls, Islamic dates and school-day reminders, never student photos without the media-consent flag; (4) who approves — proposal: Claude drafts a month of posts, the President approves the batch in one sitting, the tool schedules them. Deliverable: a one-page comparison with a recommendation and a two-week trial plan, in `marketing/social-media/`.', 'Claude explores → Muneeb (President) decides', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('71', 71, false, 'IT', '**Media-consent flags — LIVE in prod 2026-09-28** (dev `5150fa3`, prod `f025d4a`; phase 17 run in prod by the President; feature verified by Claude — student 10005''s signed form entered, badge reads "No public photos"). Student Profile shows a 📷 badge in the header ("Photos OK: public" · "Limited photo consent" · "No public photos" · "No photos at all" · "not on file") and an editable **Photo, Video & Media Consent** panel. **Remaining:** the other 14 students (10005, 10015 and 10003 entered from paper 2026-09-28; 10010 returned no consent form); until entered a student shows "not on file", which counts as no permission. Superseded in part by #73: families without an entered form are asked to fill it in the portal themselves.', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('68', 68, false, 'Marketing', 'Ask 5–10 families for Google reviews — **parked by the President until after the second school year (summer 2027)**. WhatsApp draft ready: `marketing/whatsapp/2026-09_google-review-request.md`; link comes from the profile''s "Ask for reviews" button', 'Muneeb (President)', '2027-07-01', '2027-07-01', 'Parked', null, '[{"name": "2026-09_google-review-request.md", "path": "68/2026-09_google-review-request.md", "size": 1238}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('56', 56, false, 'IT', 'Move the letter/package generators into `scripts/` as reusable tools', 'Claude', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('57', 57, false, 'IT', 'Portal hardening: `suspended` enforcement, photo-bucket policy, applicant captcha, teachers'' contact exposure', 'Claude', '2026-11-30', '2026-11-30', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('59', 59, false, 'Development', 'Fundraiser deck (`marketing/fundraiser-2026/deck/`, build with `node build.js`, data in `data.json`): **slides 11 and 12 updated 2026-10-10 at the President''s request** — expenses now five teachers $12,000 gross + employer costs $1,390 + supplies $400 = $13,790 a month; tuition $3,100 from 12 paying of 18 enrolled (6 tuition-free); gap $10,700 a month, $107,000 for the ten-month year; slide 12 reframed from "two new teachers" to "the gap to close" with the same giving ladder; **slide 13 (closing) rebuilt the same day:** target band $107,000 / $10,700 a month, "Subscribe a monthly donation" card ($50 · $100 · $300 one child''s tuition · $3,000 one teacher, recurring Zelle = sadaqah jariyah, hadith from Sahih Muslim), Zelle and enrol QR tiles. Records copy refreshed. Slide 12 footer now says the school is a 501(c)(3) and donations are tax-deductible (President''s decision 2026-10-10). **Pledge form (2026-10-10):** the President''s four-up pledge slip rebuilt as two per Letter page with the logo and a Yearly frequency option; PDF + HTML source in `records/11_Donations & Grants/02. 2026/02. General Donations/Pledge form/` (the slip carries the school''s bank account and routing numbers, so it stays in records). **Still open:** the event date on slide 1. Previous version kept as `Falah-Academy-Fundraiser-2026.bak-2026-09-19.pptx`.', 'Muneeb (President)', 'before fundraiser', null, 'In progress', null, '[{"name": "Falah-Academy-Fundraiser-2026.pptx", "path": "59/Falah-Academy-Fundraiser-2026.pptx", "size": 926039}, {"name": "Slide11-numbers-2026-10-10.png", "path": "59/Slide11-numbers-2026-10-10.png", "size": 68647}, {"name": "Slide12-ask-2026-10-10.png", "path": "59/Slide12-ask-2026-10-10.png", "size": 96471}, {"name": "Slide13-closing-2026-10-10.png", "path": "59/Slide13-closing-2026-10-10.png", "size": 210604}, {"name": "2026-10-10_Fundraiser-Pledge-Form_2-per-page.pdf", "path": "59/2026-10-10_Fundraiser-Pledge-Form_2-per-page.pdf", "size": 111096}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('60', 60, false, 'IT', 'Create the private backup repo and weekly encrypted pg_dump job per `website/supabase/OPS.md` §2; it does not exist yet (checked 2026-09-19), so the portal database has no backups', 'Muneeb (President)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('98', 98, false, 'Legal & Compliance', '**IRS Business Tax Account: Designated Official registration incomplete — re-request if wanted.** Resolved the security question: the CP311A "someone attempted to register as DO" notice (2026-06-05) was the President''s own request — the same-day CP311 letter assigned him the completion PIN, so no fraud. But the one-time PIN expired ~2026-07-05 with the envelope unopened, so the DO registration was never finished. If online access to the school''s IRS business tax account is wanted (useful for checking 941 filings and transcripts once payroll runs; not required — QBO files and EFTPS verifies), sign in at IRS.gov/BusinessAccount, re-request DO status and enter the NEW mailed PIN within 30 days of its letter. Both notices + inserts filed in `records/09_Audits & Compliance Reviews/02. IRS Correspondence/`', 'Muneeb (President)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[{"name": "2026-06-05_IRS_CP311_Designated_Official_PIN_Letter_(PIN_expired_unused).jpeg", "path": "98/2026-06-05_IRS_CP311_Designated_Official_PIN_Letter_-PIN_expired_unused-.jpeg", "size": 124916}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('99', 99, false, 'HR', '**Re-create the Pre-K assistant in QBO Payroll** (old record deleted 2026-10-05 because the name and email were wrong; correct legal name and email are in the roster note in `16_Employees/01. Employee Details/`): title Pre-K Assistant Teacher, SOC 25-9045, WA Paid Sick Leave, workers'' comp 6104-01 from 10-01, class Tuition Program, hire date 10/01/2026. **Fix the pay at the same time:** $1,000/mo salary at ~104 h is below the WA minimum ($17.13/h) — hourly at ≥ minimum for actual hours, ~$1,780/mo for 104 h, or fewer hours. Then send her Workforce invite **Minimum-wage fix (added 2026-10-10):** the Pre-K assistant is non-exempt (the teacher exemption does not cover assistants), so she must get at least **$17.13 per hour worked** (2026 WA rate; Kent has no city rate) plus overtime over 40 h/week. Current pay $1,000/month is below that: at school hours (Mon–Thu ~8:45–2:00, about 21–22 h/week ≈ 90–95 h/month) the minimum is about **$1,550–$1,650/month**. Set her up **hourly** in QBO Payroll (class 6104-01) with a simple timesheet; pay October at no less than hours × $17.13 (top up if $1,000 was already promised); confirm her real weekly hours first. Before the 2026-10-30 pay run **DECIDED 2026-10-13 (President): $1,500/month fixed salary, non-exempt, schedule Mon–Thu 9:00–2:00 = 20 h/week (no meal break needed for a 5-h shift) → regular rate $17.31/h (above $17.13).** Hours kept by exception: fixed schedule on file in her folder, only deviations noted; any hours beyond the schedule paid at $17.31 (1.5× over 40 h/week); paid sick leave accrues 1 h per 40 h. October: $1,500 (≥ 85 h × $17.13 = $1,456.05). **Re-check in December** when the 2027 WA minimum wage takes effect Jan 1 (likely above $17.31 → raise or cut hours). Open question for the President as accountant: does WA''s exempt-professional salary threshold apply to private-school lead teachers (federal teacher exemption has none) — confirm with L&I. **Steps:** (1) Claude re-creates her in QBO Payroll in the President''s signed-in browser (job title **Teaching Assistant** — President 2026-10-13, letter says "currently assigned to the Pre-K class"; salary $1,500/mo, non-exempt, 20 h/wk default, hire 10/01/2026, WA sick leave, WC 6104-01, class Tuition Program) and sends the Workforce invite; (2) she completes W-4 + direct deposit in Workforce; (3) offer letter at $1,500 with schedule — **none existed before; drafted 2026-10-13** in her `01. Contract` folder (docx + PDF, from the Pre-K teacher''s template; title Teaching Assistant; **no tuition benefit — President 2026-10-13**; letterhead footer web address corrected to falahacademywa.org) — President reviews, both sign; (4) President runs the 10/30 pay run **2026-10-13: offer letter final (no $17.31 line, footer fixed) and e-mailed with the blank I-9 by the President; WhatsApp follow-up drafted** — she signs and e-mails the letter back, brings Section 1 + original documents Thursday 10-15 **2026-10-14 QBO Payroll DONE (Claude, President signed in):** her record already existed (re-created after 10-05, correct name/e-mail, hire date 10/01/2026, monthly end-of-month schedule) and she had **already onboarded — W-4 and direct deposit on file**; Claude added job title Teaching Assistant, SOC 25-9045, salary $1,500/month with default 20 h/week (applies to all payrolls processed from now on), workers'' comp 6104-01 from 10/01/2026, WA Paid Sick Leave policy (opening balance 0); overtime pay item already present. **Left:** signed offer letter back; I-9 in person Thu 10-15; President runs the October payroll (QBO shows next payroll due **Thu 10/29**) — check her line shows $1,500 and class Tuition Program', 'Muneeb (President)', '2026-10-20', '2026-10-20', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('138', 138, false, 'IT', '**Admin edit screen for guardians and emergency contacts, plus the missing birth and immunization certificates (from #137).** (1) Claude: add edit/add/remove for guardians (name, relationship, phone, e-mail, primary/sort) and emergency contacts on the admin Students page, in dev then prod — the trigger `protect_guardian_columns` already lets signed-in admins change e-mails, while SQL-editor updates are silently reverted. First use: on 10013 move the login e-mail from the father''s guardian row to the mother''s (the login itself is already named for the mother · mother · primary). (2) Muneeb (Principal): collect the birth certificate and immunization certificate (CIS) for the six new students (one Grade 3, five Pre-K: 10011, 10004, 10013, 10014, 10008, 10012) into each `01. Admission` folder', 'Claude (screen) · Muneeb (Principal) (certificates)', '2026-10-30', '2026-10-30', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('132', 132, false, 'IT', '**Teacher mobile app (requirements, President 2026-10-11 — more to come, not urgent).** Teachers today work through Google Sheets and Forms with no portal login; this gives them one app on the phone. (1) **Sign in once** — stay signed in for a week or longer with as few re-logins as possible (long-lived session / biometric unlock). (2) **Student profiles, read-only** for their own class: name, parents'' names and phones, emergency contacts, medical conditions and allergies, photo-consent status. (3) **Mark attendance** from the phone (replaces the Sheet). (4) **Post class updates** (replaces the Google Form). (5) **Edit their own teacher profile.** Design questions for Claude before building: installable web app (PWA on the existing portal, new `teacher` role, phase SQL for teacher logins and RLS limited to the teacher''s grade) vs. a store app; how attendance-sync.gs and class-updates-form.gs retire; what the Qur''an teacher, who is already a staff login, gets. Requirements list grows here as the President adds them', 'Claude designs → Muneeb (President) decides', '2027-01-31', '2027-01-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('133', 133, false, 'IT', '**Parent mobile app (requirements, President 2026-10-11 — more to come, not urgent).** The Family Portal already does all of this in the browser; the app brings it to the phone with one sign-in and notifications. (1) **Children and profiles** — see each child''s profile and update the family information and forms. (2) **Fees** — plan, paid/unpaid months, how to pay, as on the web app. (3) **Class updates, Qur''an updates, homework and assignments.** (4) **Attendance** for each child, month calendar. Design questions for Claude before building, shared with #132: installable web app (PWA on the existing portal — the parent pages exist, so mostly install prompt, offline shell, push notifications and a long-lived session) vs. a store app; one code base for teacher and parent roles. Requirements list grows here as the President adds them', 'Claude designs → Muneeb (President) decides', '2027-01-31', '2027-01-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('134', 134, false, 'IT', '**Volunteer app (requirements, President 2026-10-12 — more to come, not urgent).** Volunteers have no portal login today; their record lives in Admin → Volunteers (#95/D50). (1) **Profile and availability** — a volunteer signs in, updates their contact details and the days/blocks they can offer (same grid as the application form). (2) **Requests** — sees the days the school has asked them to come in, the class and the teacher to report to, and can accept or decline. Office side: a "Request volunteer" action on the weekly schedule (replaces the paper Schedule & Sign-in Sheet) that notifies the volunteer. Design questions for Claude, shared with #132/#133: a `volunteer` role on the existing portal (installable web app, long-lived session) vs. a store app; one code base for teacher, parent and volunteer roles; sign-in/out from the phone to count hours. Requirements list grows here as the President adds them', 'Claude designs → Muneeb (President) decides', '2027-01-31', '2027-01-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('61', 61, false, 'HR', '**Paperwork before the 09-29 pay run and the Oct 1 payroll start:** collect a **W-9 from all five** (none on file; every one crosses the 2026 1099 threshold); write offer letters for the Pre-K assistant ($1,000) and Qur''an teacher ($3,000); **reissue the Grade 1 and KG letters at the new rates** (signed letters still say $1,000; Grade 1''s also carries a tuition waiver — confirm whether it continues); identify the empty "03. Tafla" folder. Rates set 2026-09-25. Roster + gaps: `16_Employees/01. Employee Details/2026-27_Staff_Roster_and_Paperwork_Status.md`', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-09-28', '2026-09-28', 'In progress', null, '[{"name": "w9-2023.pdf", "path": "61/w9-2023.pdf", "size": 143607}, {"name": "2026-27_Staff_Roster_and_Paperwork_Status.md", "path": "61/2026-27_Staff_Roster_and_Paperwork_Status.md", "size": 7997}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D85', 85, true, 'IT', '**Accounts owner/recovery review done and the hub''s first commit made (#51, 2026-10-13).** `docs/accounts.md` now records owner and recovery for every service: both school Google accounts — recovery phone = President''s mobile, recovery email = President''s personal Gmail, **2-step verification turned ON 2026-10-13** (was off; backup codes to print); GA4 owned by the school Gmail; Brevo has no 2-step; Facebook page, WhatsApp groups and BofA online login held by the President alone; Red Comet login on the President''s Outlook (→ #141); OneDrive on the President''s personal Microsoft account (→ #142). Analytics cleanup the same day: Umami removed, GA4 counts the live domain only, privacy page section (dev `74361c2`, prod `d384de6`); Ad Grants → #143. Hub committed locally as Falah Academy (`654e087`, 114 files, no remote; marketing exports ignored); family and donor names replaced by roles in TODO.md before the commit', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-13', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D84', 84, true, 'Students & Families', '**Contact corrections from the paper forms done in prod (#137, 2026-10-12).** SQL run and verified: missing emergency contacts added (10011, 10004, 10012, 10014, 10008, 10013), phone digits fixed, 10013 father/mother numbers swapped, 10010 mother''s name filled. Family confirmations: 10013 login = mother, now named for her · mother · PRIMARY; 10008 social + news media No (noted); 10012 name preference full name; dates of birth — the portal was right (10011 2018-06-24, 10012 2022-01-10), the paper wrong, no change. Leftover guardian e-mail move on 10013 and the missing certificates → #138. Scripts in `17_Students/02. 2026 - 2027/`', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-12', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D83', 83, true, 'Finance', '**Paid Leave + WA Cares employer account fully activated 2026-10-12 (#7).** PIN from the 09-24 letter entered (President typed it, Claude drove); account linked to SAW with **full access**, Customer ID **C605907024**, administrator = the President, contact = school Gmail/phone. The portal showed **5 past-due quarters**; with the President''s confirmation **six no-payroll reports were filed under his certification** (2025 Q2 C…2230487 · Q3 C…2322428 · Q4 C…2406137 · 2026 Q1 C…2436923 · Q2 C…2506579 · Q3 C…2535657, full numbers prefixed C605907024_20261012…): status board now all *Submitted*, next report Q4 2026 due 2027-02-01 — the first with real payroll, which QuickBooks files if the state authorisation is active (#107 checks after the 10-29 payroll). No past-due premiums (zero wages). accounts.md updated; PIN letter + status screenshot in records. Keep the paper letter. Was #7. (filed: records/03_Washington State - ESD (Unemployment)/02. Quarterly Reports/2026-10-12_PFML-WACares_Quarterly-Report-Status_all-six-no-payroll-reports-submitted.jpg)', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-12', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D82', 82, true, 'Development', '**Donations page LIVE on falahacademywa.org/donate.html (2026-10-12, dev `ceb5c59`, prod `cd202a9`, diff-dev-prod clean, verified 200 on the live site).** Page: hero with Zelle QR + copy-address button, 3-slide navy carousel (highlights / tax-deductible / employer matching "gift doubles — and so does the reward"), five Ways-to-give cards (Zelle with QR + copy-icon e-mail row; monthly jariyah $50/$100/$300/$3,000; employer matching with copy-icon Cause name + Cause ID 840-392254583 rows; sponsor a student/teacher; cheque to the office 13028 SE 231st Way), 501(c)(3)+EIN band, 3 FAQs. Zakat excluded (President: not zakat-eligible); no bank account numbers on the page. Donate link on all 16 pages (top bar, Get Involved menu, footer); 4th homepage rotator slide "Donate and Earn Lasting Reward". Wireframes on the Claude canvas "Donations Page Wireframes". **Numbers to refresh when enrollment/payroll changes: 18 students, 5 teachers, 6 tuition-free, $3,100 tuition, $13,800 cost, $10,700 gap.** Was #135.', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-12', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D81', 81, true, 'Students & Families', '**Paper forms for seven students entered in the portal (2026-10-11):** WhatsApp photos of the Medical & Allergy, Point of Contact and Photo/Media Consent forms for six students (one Grade 3, five Pre-K: 10011, 10004, 10013, 10014, 10008, 10012) plus the missing consent page for 10010 (KG) — cleaned into PDFs (`scripts/clean-forms.py`, new `gentle` mode after the first pass faded pale ink), filed in each student''s `01. Admission` folder with a `2026-10-11_Forms_Entry_Notes.md`, originals removed from Downloads. In prod: 19 digital forms entered through the admin dialog with the paper signature dates (office entry = reviewed, no red flags), 25 PDFs uploaded to Required Documents (Primary Contact, Emergency Contact, Medical/Allergies, Consent) via the Chrome extension, consent badges now show for all seven (10008 "Limited": social media and external media left blank on paper). Contact corrections that need SQL are in #131', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-11', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D80', 80, true, 'IT', '**Admin menu A–Z + coloured action counts live (#131) — 2026-10-10:** Dashboard first, other items sorted A–Z at render (new items place themselves); "Label (n)" beside items with work waiting — Admissions under review, Volunteers new, Feedback unresolved, Students photos + parent-edited forms to review, Attendance grades unmarked after 10 AM on school days, Class Updates since last visit; **Tasks (red, orange)** in red/orange, **Fees (paid, unpaid)** in green/red (Dashboard rule); colours turn white on the active item. `lib/menuCounts.ts` + `layouts/AdminLayout.tsx`. Dev b2a8f26/59c2362/95c3703, prod f78df0a, bundle index-D6iXCE82.js live; checked on dev by the President', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D79', 79, true, 'HR', '**Volunteer call posted on WhatsApp (#97)** — President launched the messages from `marketing/whatsapp/2026-10_volunteer-call.md` (link falahacademywa.org/volunteer.html); watch Admin → Volunteers for applications', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D78', 78, true, 'IT', '**Dev Supabase e-mail mirrored and tested (#58) — 2026-10-10:** URL config already right; custom SMTP ON in dev like prod (Brevo smtp-relay.brevo.com:587, sender Falah Academy <falahacademywa@gmail.com>, 30/h). First test failed `535 Authentication failed` (wrong key type) — President pasted a Brevo **SMTP** key (xsmtpsib-…) and it worked: Forgot-password e-mail to the new dev test login `falahacademywa+devtest@gmail.com` arrived in the school inbox via Brevo, link goes to the dev project. Return-path quirk logged as #130', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D77', 77, true, 'Marketing', '**Search engines set up (#26) — 2026-10-10:** HTTPS enforced; Google Search Console sitemap resubmitted (owner falahacademywa@gmail.com); **Bing Webmaster Tools**: President signed in with the school Google account, site imported from Search Console (view-only consent), sitemap read — Success, 14 URLs. Both recorded in `docs/accounts.md`', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D76', 76, true, 'Marketing', '**Google Business Profile finished (#24) — 2026-10-10:** categories set by the President to **Primary school (primary), Religious school, Preschool** (no pending edit left; Google has no "Private school" category); opening date September 2025; description, phone, website, Facebook link in place; verified. Photos stay parked with #66, reviews with #68 (filed: marketing/google-business-profile.md)', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D75', 75, true, 'Finance', '**Intuit subscription 10-01 $220.80 posted (#86) — 2026-10-10:** from the …8048 feed (card ending 0039) to Software Subscriptions, class Administration, vendor Intuit QuickBooks Online. The Intuit receipt (invoice 10001533469539) lists Workforce Payroll, a payroll worker charge and QBO Plus but no per-item amounts, so no split was possible', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D74', 74, true, 'Finance', '**Payment receipts sent to one family (#123) — 2026-10-10:** three receipts (2026-06-01 $500 sibling rate, 2026-09-08 $300, 2026-10-01 $300) generated with `scripts/make-receipt.py`, checked against the Zelle alerts and QBO, signed electronically by the President, filed in the Pre-K student''s `02. Fees` folder and e-mailed by the President from the school Gmail (draft prepared by Claude). The 10-01 $300 still to be recorded in QBO under #125', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D73', 73, true, 'Finance', '**$1,260 cleared from QBO "Payments to deposit" (#126) — 2026-10-10:** the family''s cash lump sum of 2026-03-03 (sales receipt 1034) had been held by the President; he sent it to the school by Zelle on 10-10 (conf. p1zthyd6m). Recorded as a Bank Deposit to …8048 dated 10-10 using receipt 1034 (memo explains it). Balance sheet as of 10-10: Payments to deposit $0.00, …8048 in QBO $6,031.57. The bank-feed line must be matched to this deposit (#125)', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D72', 72, true, 'Finance', '**September 2026 close completed (#124) — 2026-10-10.** Reconciliation and postings were done 2026-10-06 (…8048 and …9334 reconciled to 09-30, difference $0.00; all eight September tuition payments matched bank ↔ portal ↔ QBO; donations and expenses posted — `08_Financials/02. 2026/05. Revenue Reports/2026-10-06_September-2026_Close_Note.md`). Today: September P&L (revenue $10,400.00, expenditures $8,343.28, net +$2,056.72) and 09-30 Balance Sheet (total assets $7,069.57) filed as `08_Financials/02. 2026/06. QuickBooks Exports/2026-09-30_September-2026_P&L_and_Balance_Sheet.md`. Loose end → #{n}', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D71', 71, true, 'Finance', '**2025–26 fees sheet reconciled with QBO and the bank (#122) — 2026-10-10:** 2025 bank Zelle $7,500 = QBO $7,500 = sheet $7,500. Sheet fixes: one family''s Sep-2025 row and the seven unpaid Oct 2025–Apr 2026 rows now = their $1,260 cash lump sum of 2026-03-03 (QBO receipt 1034; $300 + $960 spread evenly, $137.14 a month, special discount per the President); four paid Summer 2026 rows dated from the Zelle alerts (= QBO Summer Program Fees $800); six unpaid Summer 2026 rows deleted. Rule added to `docs/bookkeeping.md`: record tuition in QBO on the date received. Follow-up the same day: that family''s missing June 2026 row added ($300 Zelle received 06-05; QBO deposit 06-08). Sheet backup in the session scratchpad', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D70', 70, true, 'Finance', '**2025 fees sheet vs QBO checked (#36) — 2026-10-10:** QBO FY2025 revenue **$7,500** (Tuition $6,900 + Zakat $600) = the Fees sheet''s 2025-dated "paid" rows exactly ($7,500). FY2025 990-N (≤ $50,000) is safe either way. Monthly split differs (QBO Sep 2,100 / Oct 1,800 / Nov 1,500 / Dec 2,100 vs sheet by payment date 2,400 / 1,800 / 2,700 / 600) — QBO dates follow neither payment date nor billing month exactly. Open points moved to #122', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-10', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('D69', 69, true, 'IT', '**Qur''an and academic progress dated in Pacific time (#118, UTC audit item 3) — 2026-10-09:** Admin → Academics sends `assessment_date: todayStr()`; phase 24 sets both `assessment_date` defaults to the Pacific date (run in dev and prod by the President, verified). Dev `f54de01`, prod `92bedd3`, bundle `index-ZnQoCgtn.js` live', '', '', null, 'Done', '2026-10-09', '[]'::jsonb, now()),
